course: dictionary
lesson: 9879
title: A planned move
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A tactic is a planned action or method that you use to get a result. It is a plan with a purpose. In «Explaining each side is like a referee who knows both teams' tactics without wearing either shirt», the referee knows the plans each team uses to try to win, even though he is not on either team.
explain: Tactic is often used in sport. Coaches talk about tactics such as passing, defending and attacking, which are ways of arranging and moving players to win a game. Soldiers in a battle also use tactics. In a story, a character might try a new tactic to solve a problem.
explain: Context helps you here. Ask yourself what the plan is for. If the word "plan" or "method" fits the sentence, your guess is probably right. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and read it again to check.
fact: A tactic is a planned action or method used to get a result.
fact: «Tactics» (the plural) can mean the way players or soldiers are arranged and moved to win a game or a battle.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «a clever tactic», «change tactics», «scare tactics» and «delaying tactic».
fact: In maths, a tactic can be a way to solve a problem, such as drawing a diagram or working backwards.
fact: Tactic is a noun. Its plural is tactics.
exercise: The coach changed tactics at half time, and the team passed the ball more. What does tactics mean here? | *Planned ways of playing to win | Scores at the end of the game | Shoes worn for football | Long, boring speeches
exercise: What does a tactic mean? | A type of weather | A random accident that nobody planned | *A planned action or method used to get a result | A sports shirt with a number on it
exercise: «Explaining each side is like a referee who knows both teams' tactics without wearing either shirt.» Who knows the tactics? | The shirt maker | The players wearing the shirts | *The referee | The crowd cheering
test: In a story, Sam tries a new tactic to solve his problem. What is a tactic in this sentence? | A bag he carries to school | *A planned method he uses to get a result | A loud noise | A type of food
test: Which word is the plural of tactic? | tactician | tactic's | *tactics | tactical
exam: Read: «Explaining each side is like a referee who knows both teams' tactics.» What are the teams' tactics most like? | Their favourite snacks | Their colours | *Their planned methods for winning | Their coach's car
